meta {
  name: Assign vehicle/driver/workflow (workaround via PATCH)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{lastOrderId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "vehicle_id": "{{lastVehicleId}}",
    "driver_id": "{{lastDriverId}}",
    "workflow_id": "{{lastWorkflowId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  # Asignar recursos a una orden

  **Backend NO tiene endpoints dedicados:**
  - `POST /orders/:id/assign-vehicle` → 405
  - `POST /orders/:id/assign-driver` → 405
  - `POST /orders/:id/assign-workflow` → 404
  - `PUT /orders/:id` → 405 (no acepta PUT en orders)

  **Workaround:** usar `PATCH /orders/:id` con los FKs en el body.

  Campos validos para asignar:
  - `vehicle_id`   → asigna vehiculo
  - `driver_id`    → asigna conductor
  - `workflow_id`  → asigna workflow (si el backend lo persiste)
  - `operator_id`  → asigna operador logistico

  Backend responde 200 con el shape completo de la orden actualizada en `{data: {...}}`.
}
